#%PAM-1.0
# Ryoku in-session lock — FINGERPRINT conversation
#
# One of the lock screen's TWO parallel PAM conversations (see
# ryoku-lock-pw for the password one). Loaded by PamContext.configDirectory
# from the lock's own assets/pam/, so NO root edit of /etc/pam.d is needed.
#
# WHY TWO FILES: pam_fprintd's man page is explicit — the PAM stack is
# serialised by design, so parallel methods (fingerprint + password) must
# run in separate conversations, "the way multiple authentication methods
# are made available to users of gdm". In a single conversation the
# password prompt starved the sensor: the default 30s scan timeout fell
# through to pam_unix, the conversation stayed alive waiting for a typed
# key, and the lock never re-armed the scan (touch stopped working).
#
# timeout=-1: keep scanning for the whole lock instead of giving up after
# the default 30s; max-tries (default 3) still ends the conversation on
# repeated misreads so the UI can flash "Not recognized" and re-arm.
#
# MODULE STACK:
#   auth  sufficient  pam_fprintd.so timeout=-1   <- touch-to-unlock
#   auth  required    pam_deny.so                 <- 3 misreads ⇒ fail ⇒ re-arm
#   account required  pam_unix.so                 <- account validation
#   password required pam_deny.so                 <- no password changes
#   session required  pam_unix.so                 <- session setup

auth        sufficient  pam_fprintd.so timeout=-1
auth        required    pam_deny.so
account     required    pam_unix.so
password    required    pam_deny.so
session     required    pam_unix.so
